  "requiredChecks": [
    "Verify each originally valid program before either route; record each checked stage result and require it valid.",
    "For every valid intermediate compare its internal helper result with its public checked stage exactly; require validity, no input mutation, same retained function order, and all direct/address references resolved.",
    "Compare full final NxProgram/JSON and complete emitted C and QBE products, not a tiny hash or runtime checksum alone. Record file hashes as identities after byte equality.",
    "Reuse all finite independent scalar/tail/leaf/memory complete-output expectations. Honor native-only deep-tail inputs; never execute recursive refusal or malformed input.",
    "For invalid inputs with a foldable constant expression require exact identity from the boundary-guarded reference and candidate; malformed structure must not enter private transforms.",
    "Every capacity refusal is stage-local. Compare exact output to the checked composition rather than asserting the whole large program stays unchanged.",
    "Compare fresh parameter snapshots, local resets, collision avoidance, shared demand fuel, original callee bodies, branch order, aliases, store/free/unknown-call effects, and zero-trip loops through unchanged existing control oracles.",
    "On an isolated verification-failure injection into the final candidate, nx_r_finish must return exact original; separately reject any intermediate-validity failure instead of treating final validity as a semantic proof."
  ],
